<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nasr Al-Madhkur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Nasir Al Madhkur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nasr Al-Madhkur was the Arab sheikh of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bushehr">Bushehr</a> on the Persian coast of the Gulf in the mid-18th century, governing in the name of the Persian state. He extended his family's power across the Gulf by taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a> in 1753. His governor there was driven out in 1783 by the Al <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bani-utbah">Bani Utbah</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zubarah">Zubarah</a>, ending Bushehr's rule over the islands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nasr-al-madhkur.jpg" alt="Nasr Al-Madhkur" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Walker, John · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapofqatar1849.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
